  "scope": "Three independent 16-rank NPU-only windows, seven complete target-to-next-target periods per rank. Same 2 verification argmax, 6 draft HcPre/HcPost, 3 draft expert and 5 draft score argmax sites in every period. After the last draft argmax, the first observed next metadata kernel is identified by native type. All edges are device-local chronological markers. The named-task-count field is a count; durations are ms.",
  "uses": "Determine which phase changes with prior accepted CP/slot/CPU-plan work and which QLI work still executes. No combined QLI+CPUplan arm has been measured. Differences of medians across runs need not add and are not causal speedups.",
  "limits": "Intervals without a recorded kernel or DMA can contain host scheduling, submission, dependencies or other activity. The derived gap is not a quantity one can remove. Chronological endpoints do not establish independence or identify the last reader. Timings are profiled.",
